msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.docstrings.DocstringCoverage.ratio:1 of
msgid "A root holding no public object is fully documented, not undocumented."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.docstrings.DocstringCoverage.ratio:3 of
msgid ""
"There is nothing in it anybody failed to write about. Reading that as 0 %"
" would refuse a commit to a package that has nothing wrong with it."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.docstrings.DocstringCoverage.undocumented:1 of
msgid ""
"The objects holding the figure down, qualified name and line, in file "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.docstrings.is_public:3 of
msgid ""
"A leading underscore means private and is not counted, in either "
"direction: an undocumented helper does not lower the figure, and "
"documenting one does not raise it. ``__init__`` and its siblings are the "
"exception — they are public behaviour written in a private-looking "
"spelling, and a class whose constructor is undocumented is a class whose "
"constructor is undocumented."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.docstrings.module_name_for:3 of
msgid ""
"``__init__.py`` takes its package's name rather than becoming "
"``package.__init__``, so that the per-module breakdown reads the way an "
"import statement does."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.docstrings.walk_module:3 of
msgid ""
"A file that does not parse yields nothing and says so through the "
"exception, which the caller turns into a finding: a syntax error is the "
"linter's news to break, not this command's, and a documentation figure "
"that silently drops a file would be a figure about a different codebase."
msgstr ""

